            {
                "content": "# DREWS CREEK RESERVOIR NEAR LAKEVIEW, OREG.\n\n- LOCATION.-Dam is in sec. 5, T. 40 S., R. 18 E., about 14 miles southwest of Lakeview; reservoir is about 10 miles in length.\n\n- RECORDS AVAILABLE. - -February 26 to September 30, 1913.\n\nGage.-Readings obtained by measuring down from the floor of the gate house. Gage datum is lowest contour of reservoir.\n\nOUTLETS.--A tunnel with sill at elevation 16.3 feet, and a blow-out pipe in center of dam at bottom.\n\n- STORAGE.-Reservoir was filled up to outlet tunnel during winter of 1911-12, but was practically empty October 1, 1912. The rate of filling between that date and March 31, 1913, has been estimated.\n\n- Accuracy.-Monthly estimates of increase or decrease in volume of storage are only approximate, as the readings of water stage are very rough, but the error for the entire year is probably not great.\n\nDaily gage height, in feet, of Drews Creek reservoir near Lakeview, Oreg., for the year ending Sept. 30, 1913.",
